+# The Daily Grind
+
+A static homepage built with native Web Components. No runtime dependencies or build step are required. Load `components/daily-grind.js` as a module and use the elements in any page. Each component owns its styles in an open Shadow DOM.
+
+- `<site-navigation>`: site links and a mobile disclosure menu with Escape handling and focus return.
+- `<coffee-hero>`: hero with optional `heading`, `eyebrow`, and default description slots.
+- `<coffee-menu>`: seasonal section containing slotted `<coffee-card>` elements. All/Warm/Cold buttons filter by the cards' `category` attributes. Filter results are announced through a polite live region.
+- `<coffee-card>`: accepts `name`, `description`, `category` (`warm` or `cold`), `image`, `image-alt`, `badge`, `notes`, and `href`. Attributes update reactively. Notes use native `<details>`; omit `notes` to hide that control. Give meaningful photos an `image-alt`; omit it for decorative photos. Use trusted image and link URLs.
+- `<site-footer>`: footer navigation and copyright.
+
+```html
+<coffee-menu>
+  <coffee-card
+    name="Cold Brew"
+    category="cold"
+    description="Steeped for 18 hours for maximum smoothness."
+    notes="Smooth, rounded, and refreshing."
+    href="/menu/cold-brew">
+  </coffee-card>
+</coffee-menu>
+```
+
+Components inherit the page font and support the `--primary`, `--paper`, and `--focus` CSS properties with built-in defaults. Keep a visible focus color with sufficient contrast. Component event listeners are cleaned up when disconnected. The menu handles new cards and category changes while a filter is active.
+
+Run `pnpm install` and `pnpm test` for DOM tests covering component registration, original navigation destinations, attribute updates, filter state and announcements, Escape focus return, and reconnection. Tests do not start a server or browser. Native browser layout and assistive technology behavior are outside these tests.
